§§ `s 21ZA tests`
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`no holidays` MEANS EMPTY

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`only 28 Dec 2026 is a bank holiday` MEANS LIST (Date 28 12 2026)

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`only Friday 6 Nov 2026 is a bank holiday` MEANS LIST (Date 6 11 2026)

-- s 21ZA(4) "a day other than a Saturday, a Sunday, Christmas Day, Good Friday or a day that is a bank holiday"
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(4) the day is a working day` (Date 6 11 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(4) the day is a working day` (Date 7 11 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(4) the day is a working day` (Date 8 11 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(4) the day is a working day` (Date 9 11 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(4) the day is a working day` (Date 24 12 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(4) the day is a working day` (Date 25 12 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(4) the day is a working day` (Date 28 12 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(4) the day is a working day` (Date 28 12 2026) `only 28 Dec 2026 is a bank holiday` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(4) the day is a working day` (Date 29 12 2026) `only 28 Dec 2026 is a bank holiday` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- the helper: the first working day counting from Sat 7 Nov is Mon 9 Nov; the seventh counting from Mon 9 Nov is Tue 17 Nov
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(3) the working day numbered` 1 `counting from` (Date 7 11 2026) `and` `no holidays` EQUALS Date 9 11 2026
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(3) the working day numbered` 7 `counting from` (Date 9 11 2026) `and` `no holidays` EQUALS Date 17 11 2026
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(3) the working day numbered` 1 `counting from` (Date 9 11 2026) `and` `no holidays` EQUALS Date 9 11 2026
-- s 21ZA(3) "the period of 7 working days starting with the first working day after the person makes the disclosure": the last day is the seventh working day, the first counted as 1
-- Disclosed Mon 2 Nov: Tue 3 (1), Wed 4 (2), Thu 5 (3), Fri 6 (4), Mon 9 (5), Tue 10 (6), Wed 11 (7)
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(3) the last day of the notice period` (Date 2 11 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS Date 11 11 2026
-- one day earlier or later is a different answer
#ASSERT NOT (`s 21ZA(3) the last day of the notice period` (Date 2 11 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS Date 10 11 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 21ZA(3) the last day of the notice period` (Date 2 11 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS Date 12 11 2026)
-- Disclosed Thu 5 Nov: Fri 6 (1), Mon 9 (2), Tue 10 (3), Wed 11 (4), Thu 12 (5), Fri 13 (6), Mon 16 (7)
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(3) the last day of the notice period` (Date 5 11 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS Date 16 11 2026
-- Disclosed Fri 6 Nov: the first working day after is Mon 9 (1), Tue 10 (2), Wed 11 (3), Thu 12 (4), Fri 13 (5), Mon 16 (6), Tue 17 (7)
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(3) the last day of the notice period` (Date 6 11 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS Date 17 11 2026
-- Disclosed on Sat 7 Nov: the first working day after is Mon 9; the same last day, Tue 17
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(3) the last day of the notice period` (Date 7 11 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS Date 17 11 2026
-- Disclosed Mon 2 Nov with Fri 6 Nov a bank holiday: Tue 3 (1), Wed 4 (2), Thu 5 (3), Mon 9 (4), Tue 10 (5), Wed 11 (6), Thu 12 (7)
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(3) the last day of the notice period` (Date 2 11 2026) `only Friday 6 Nov 2026 is a bank holiday` EQUALS Date 12 11 2026
-- Straddling Christmas.  Disclosed Mon 21 Dec 2026: Tue 22 (1), Wed 23 (2), Thu 24 (3), Fri 25 is Christmas Day, Sat 26 and Sun 27 are the weekend, Mon 28 (4), Tue 29 (5), Wed 30 (6), Thu 31 (7)
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(3) the last day of the notice period` (Date 21 12 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS Date 31 12 2026
-- the same, with Mon 28 Dec a bank holiday: Tue 29 (4), Wed 30 (5), Thu 31 (6), Fri 1 Jan 2027 (7)
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(3) the last day of the notice period` (Date 21 12 2026) `only 28 Dec 2026 is a bank holiday` EQUALS Date 1 1 2027

-- s 21ZA(2) "treated as having an authorised officer's consent if before the end of the notice period the person does not receive notice that consent is refused"
-- Disclosed Mon 2 Nov: the notice period ends on Wed 11 Nov 2026.  Arguments: disclosure day, holidays, day the refusal was received, day I am asking about
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(2) the person is treated as having the authorised officer's consent` (Date 2 11 2026) `no holidays` (JUST (Date 3 11 2026)) (Date 20 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(2) the person is treated as having the authorised officer's consent` (Date 2 11 2026) `no holidays` (JUST (Date 2 11 2026)) (Date 20 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a refusal received on the last day of the period is received before the period ends
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(2) the person is treated as having the authorised officer's consent` (Date 2 11 2026) `no holidays` (JUST (Date 11 11 2026)) (Date 20 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a refusal received the day after the last day comes too late
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(2) the person is treated as having the authorised officer's consent` (Date 2 11 2026) `no holidays` (JUST (Date 12 11 2026)) (Date 20 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a refusal that pre-dates the disclosure is not a refusal of it
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(2) the person is treated as having the authorised officer's consent` (Date 2 11 2026) `no holidays` (JUST (Date 1 11 2026)) (Date 20 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no refusal: on the last day, or before it, the period has not ended and the "if" is not met (ruling of 2026-11-05, (a); fork F3), so JUST FALSE; the day after it, JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(2) the person is treated as having the authorised officer's consent` (Date 2 11 2026) `no holidays` NOTHING (Date 11 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(2) the person is treated as having the authorised officer's consent` (Date 2 11 2026) `no holidays` NOTHING (Date 9 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(2) the person is treated as having the authorised officer's consent` (Date 2 11 2026) `no holidays` NOTHING (Date 12 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- with Fri 6 Nov a bank holiday the period ends Thu 12 Nov, so on Thu 12 Nov it has not ended (JUST FALSE) and on Fri 13 Nov it has (JUST TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(2) the person is treated as having the authorised officer's consent` (Date 2 11 2026) `only Friday 6 Nov 2026 is a bank holiday` NOTHING (Date 12 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(2) the person is treated as having the authorised officer's consent` (Date 2 11 2026) `only Friday 6 Nov 2026 is a bank holiday` NOTHING (Date 13 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Prior consent facts columns: involved, disclosed before becoming involved, has the authorised officer's consent
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(1) the person does not commit an offence under any of sections 15 to 18 by involvement, having disclosed first and had consent` (`Prior consent facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(1) the person does not commit an offence under any of sections 15 to 18 by involvement, having disclosed first and had consent` (`Prior consent facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(1) the person does not commit an offence under any of sections 15 to 18 by involvement, having disclosed first and had consent` (`Prior consent facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(1) the person does not commit an offence under any of sections 15 to 18 by involvement, having disclosed first and had consent` (`Prior consent facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(5) the person is an authorised officer` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(5) the person is an authorised officer` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(6) the involvement is in a transaction or arrangement relating to money or other property` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(6) the involvement is in a transaction or arrangement relating to money or other property` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21ZA(6) the involvement is in a transaction or arrangement relating to money or other property` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

